<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_SumpDuskLock_BiomeWiring.xml       UtinniPatches · SUMP_MECHANICS_1 (S6)
  ============================================================================
  Wires the permanent dusk lock (Defs/GameConditionDefs/RUT_SumpDuskLock.xml)
  onto RUT_Sump as a PATCH rather than a direct edit to RUT_Sump.xml's own
  biomeMapConditions field  — RUT_SumpDuskLock only exists when
  mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards is active (MayRequire-gated Def), so a
  bare <li> baked directly into the always-loaded BiomeDef would be a
  dangling cross-reference the moment that mod is absent. Gate:
  PatchOperationFindMod on the kit's display name. ⚠️ MayRequire on an
  <Operation> is INERT (MEASURED 2026-09-17 against 1.6 source —
  ModContentPack.LoadPatches never reads the attribute); this operation's
  own xpath (targeting our always-loaded RUT_Sump) does not depend on the
  gated mod either, so without a real gate it would run every load and
  inject the dangling reference regardless. FindMod is the only real
  per-operation gate. Exact precedent: RUT_ScaldSteamLock_BiomeWiring.xml,
  this same folder, same pass window.

  RUT_Sump.xml carries no <biomeMapConditions> node at all today (only
  wildAnimals/baseWeatherCommonalities/terrainsByFertility/diseases), so this
  adds the whole element rather than appending an <li> to an existing one.

  THESUMP_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 (Phase A, 2026-09-25): this file physically moved
  from src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches into src/RimMandrake/TheSump, defName
  target and content otherwise UNCHANGED — it still wires RUT_SumpDuskLock
  onto RUT_Sump alone. The new standalone RM_TheSump def gets the SAME
  RUT_SumpDuskLock condition baked directly into its own biomeMapConditions
  (RM_TheSump_Biome.xml), not a second patch op here — biome_mod_
  architecture.md §5 step 4 offers either shape ("a second op... or bake it
  natively... now that it's a same-mod dependency"); baking it matches the
  precedent MIASMA_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 actually shipped (RM_Miasma.xml's own
  biomeMapConditions lists RUT_MiasmaWeatherLock inline, no patch needed,
  since the condition def now lives in the SAME mod as the biome). One
  GameConditionDef, one WeatherDef (both moved here with defNames unchanged),
  read by both biome instances.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimMandrake: Environmental Hazards Kit</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RUT_Sump"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <biomeMapConditions>
          <li>RUT_SumpDuskLock</li>
        </biomeMapConditions>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
